{"name":"Alluring Gesture","hex":"#f8dbc2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alluring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the power to allure."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or habit of enticing or attracting in order to seek a benefit or advantage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alluring"},{"term":"gesture","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A motion of the limbs or body, especially one made to emphasize speech.","An act or a remark that serves as a formality or as a sign of attitude."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a gesture or gestures.","To express (something) by a gesture or gestures."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gesture"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gesture","blocks":[{"text":"A gesture is a form of nonverbal communication or non-vocal communication in which visible bodily actions communicate particular messages, either in place of, or in conjunction with, speech. Gestures include movement of the hands, face, or other parts of the body. Gestures differ from physical non-verbal communication that does not communicate specific messages, such as purely expressive displays, proxemics, or displays of joint attention. Gestures allow individuals to communicate a variety of feelings and thoughts, from contempt and hostility to approval and affection, often together with body language in addition to words when they speak. Gesticulation and speech work independently of each other, but join to provide emphasis and meaning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Madonna_%40_Berlinale_%281%29_cropped.jpg/330px-Madonna_%40_Berlinale_%281%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gesture"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Us_navy_helicopter_landing_signals_illustration.jpg/500px-Us_navy_helicopter_landing_signals_illustration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Us_navy_helicopter_landing_signals_illustration.jpg/500px-Us_navy_helicopter_landing_signals_illustration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Military air marshallers use hand and body gestures to direct flight operations aboard aircraft carriers.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUs_navy_helicopter_landing_signals_illustration.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Plate_I_%28The_Sign_Language_2nd_ed._1918%29.png/500px-Plate_I_%28The_Sign_Language_2nd_ed._1918%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Plate_I_%28The_Sign_Language_2nd_ed._1918%29.png/500px-Plate_I_%28The_Sign_Language_2nd_ed._1918%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1918 picture dictionary of American Sign Language","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlate_I_(The_Sign_Language_2nd_ed._1918).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/VitarkaMudra.JPG/250px-VitarkaMudra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b3/VitarkaMudra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/VitarkaMudra.JPG/250px-VitarkaMudra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vitarka Vicara, Tarim Basin, 9th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVitarkaMudra.JPG"}],"sounds":{"alluring":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-alluring.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=r